=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  ports ufw-inactive -------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Proposed: no Figma frame. web-01.example.net listens on 22, 80$
# and 443 on every address, 5353/udp, 5432 on loopback alone,$
# 9090 and 9100. ufw is installed and not running, so nothing is$
# filtered: every port but the loopback one says so, and a saved$
# rule's port with nothing listening has no row.$
$
# Firewall Settings ############################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Review ~ inactive$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  [::]:22              Not filtered$
   -  0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow Saved$
  [+] 80/tcp               Allow Saved$
  [+] 443/tcp              Allow Saved$
  [+] 8080/tcp             Allow Saved$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow Saved$
  [+] 80/tcp (v6)          Allow Saved$
  [+] 443/tcp (v6)         Allow Saved$
  [+] 8080/tcp (v6)        Allow Saved$
$
  Ports --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  22/tcp               Not filtered sshd$
   -  80/tcp               Not filtered nginx$
   -  443/tcp              Not filtered nginx$
   -  5353/udp             Not filtered avahi-daemon$
   -  5432/tcp             Local only postgres$
   -  9090/tcp             Not filtered prometheus$
   -  9100/tcp             Not filtered node_exporter$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]:$
$
$

